Note that, even if a patch doesn't originally have #ifdef's, you can
add them while applying the patch by using patch -D.

In fact, it's harder to remove the #ifdef's from a patch that has them
than to add them to one that doesn't.

(Of course, this is all assuming the files you're patching are C code.)

